- a#14 'TWD 1.57M' -> 'TWD 1,57 juta': REVERTED. src/data/__tests__/guidance-team-bios.test.ts asserts every string in GUIDANCE_BIO_PRESERVED_TERMS (which includes 'TWD 1.57M') appears byte-identical in EVERY locale's bio. That constant is cross-locale, not an Indonesian string, so it is out of this lane's write scope. The bio keeps 'TWD 1.57M'. Needs a supervisor decision if the juta form is wanted.
- a#19 'Menu': test src/lib/__tests__/guidance-chrome-language.test.ts guards `menuLabel !== 'Menu'` (that literal is the English fallback it detects). Used 'Menu navigasi' instead — Indonesian, and not the fallback string.
- a#31 / b#18 empty `​` (ZWSP) padding blocks in 003/005/013/015: NOT removed. The checker compares ZWSP counts and non-empty block counts against the source (003 has 52 ZWSP, 005 has 8, 013 has 5); deleting them fails `blocks`. Left in place.
- b#33 018 renumber '## 7.' -> '## 6.' (and 8 -> 7): REVERTED. The checker's `numbers` lane compares digit tokens against the Korean source and reported `missing from translation (1): 8 / extra in translation (1): 6` -> FAIL. Per the rulebook ("prefer the form the checker accepts"), the source's 7/8 numbering is kept. The same outline gap exists in columns-en/018; it is a source-side bug for the supervisor.

## 4. Where I disagree with the reviewer (not applied as written)
- a#4 (llms discoveryNotice). Applied 'dukungan' -> 'pengesahan' (endorsement) — correct. Did NOT apply 'jaminan untuk ditampilkan' -> 'pemuatan iklan'. The English source reads "it does not promise search ranking, endorsement, AI recommendation, or guaranteed visibility", and vi/th render the same concept as display/visibility ("việc được hiển thị", "การแสดงผล"). 'Pemuatan iklan' (ad placement) would change the meaning to something the source does not say. Kept 'jaminan untuk ditampilkan'.
- a#13. Reviewer wanted 'para hakim konstitusi'; ACCEPTED-id specifies 'para Hakim Agung Mahkamah Konstitusi (大法官)'. Followed ACCEPTED.
- a#17. Reviewer wanted 'bidang praktik'; ACCEPTED-id specifies 'bidang layanan' (and it matches the existing nav label). Followed ACCEPTED.
- b#30. Reviewer wanted 'TWD 30.000.000'; used 'TWD 30 juta' so the amount is unchanged AND the checker's number parity with the source ('30') is preserved. Same for 'TWD 100 juta'.
- b#11/b#4/b#25. Reviewer sometimes proposed replacing the heading; I made the first sentence self-standing instead, because the rulebook forbids changing the heading count/structure and the headings are shared with the other locales' outline.
- b#20. Reviewer's rewrite would merge two blocks; the checker compares block counts, so I moved the break instead of removing it.
- Note on the frontmatter FAQ blocks: where the frontmatter `q:` really is a yes/no question (008 ×2, 011, 014, 017 ×2), the 'Tidak./Bukan.' opening is correct and was kept; only the body leads under topic headings were rewritten.

